{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-video-watch  (2026-10-20, Webster)
  The watch page for ONE video: /pages/<handle>, template page.video.
  The video is the main content of the page (title, then the player in
  the first viewport), which is what Google needs to show the page as a
  video result. The paired field notes post stays a different angle on
  the same idea and links here, it is not replaced.

  Which video: the record in snippets/theinmag-videos-data whose handle
  equals page.handle. If nothing matches (only ever a draft preview via
  ?view=video on another page), it falls back to the preview_handle
  setting, then the first record.

  Before live_from: poster + "out <day>" on a scrim, no iframe, no
  VideoObject. The real iframe sits in a <template> and a small script
  swaps it in once the time passes, so a cached page never stays stale.
  After live_from: a real youtube-nocookie iframe (crawlable embed, no
  facade, deliberately: this is a video-result page) + VideoObject.

  Transcript: the page's own content (paste the cleaned .srt text into
  the page body in admin). It renders in a <details>, and its plain
  text goes into VideoObject.transcript.

  Hub, ItemList and the "more videos" row live in other sections; this
  file only knows its own video.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  capture vdata
    render 'theinmag-videos-data'
  endcapture
  assign records = vdata | strip | split: '@@'
  assign now_num = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0

  assign rec = ''
  assign matched = false
  for r in records
    assign rh = r | split: '^^' | first | strip
    if rh == page.handle
      assign rec = r
      assign matched = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if rec == blank and section.settings.preview_handle != blank
    for r in records
      assign rh = r | split: '^^' | first | strip
      if rh == section.settings.preview_handle
        assign rec = r
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if rec == blank
    assign rec = records | first
  endif

  assign f = rec | split: '^^'
  assign v_handle = f[0] | strip
  assign v_id = f[1]
  assign v_show = f[2]
  assign v_title = f[3]
  assign v_live_iso = f[4]
  assign v_live_ts = f[4] | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign v_live_label = f[5]
  assign v_duration = f[6]
  assign v_minutes = f[7]
  assign v_thumb = f[8]
  assign v_summary = f[10]
  assign v_points = f[11] | split: ';;'
  assign v_kid = f[12]
  assign v_post = f[13]
  assign v_area = f[14]

  assign is_coming = false
  if section.settings.preview_as_live != true and now_num < v_live_ts
    assign is_coming = true
  endif

  if v_show == 'picnic'
    assign show_name = 'Picnic Planning'
    assign show_anchor = '/pages/videos#picnic-planning'
  else
    assign show_name = 'Field Notes'
    assign show_anchor = '/pages/videos#field-notes'
  endif

  assign thumb_large = v_thumb | append: '.jpg' | asset_url
  assign embed_src = 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/' | append: v_id | append: '?rel=0&amp;playsinline=1&amp;enablejsapi=1'
  assign watch_url = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' | append: v_id
  assign page_url = shop.url | append: '/pages/' | append: v_handle

  assign transcript_html = ''
  if matched and page.content != blank
    assign transcript_html = page.content
  endif

  comment
    Magazine look (2026-11-05): Post is all caps, so a standalone word
    "in" would print as a lifted IN outside theINmag (house rule). Any
    line that contains one falls back to Inter. Check is on the padded,
    lower-cased, punctuation-stripped text.
  endcomment
  assign cover_product = all_products[section.settings.mag_cover_handle]

  comment
    The red tape carries the kid's question, never just a credit. The
    question is the summary's first sentence when it ends in "?" (the
    summary is written from the video, so nothing is invented); the rest
    of the summary shows below it. No question, no tape: the credit
    stays a plain line.
  endcomment
  comment
    10 Nov 2026, Ryan: the kid's question drives the lesson but must not be the headline of the
    page, so the summary is never split into a pulled-out question any more. Summaries now open
    with the adult's own search question (see VIDEO-RELEASE-FORMAT.md) and the credit stays a
    plain line.
  endcomment
  assign v_question = ''
  assign summary_rest = v_summary
  assign q_clean = v_question | downcase | replace: ',', ' ' | replace: '?', ' '
  assign q_padded = ' ' | append: q_clean | append: ' '
  assign q_post = true
  if q_padded contains ' in '
    assign q_post = false
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Simplified look (2026-11-06, Ryan: "I like the simplified style ... run with that"), the same language
  as the field notes post video band: the series ground on top (Picnic = forest green with faint rings
  and dots; Field Notes = the blog index's peach pattern), video left, the way on right; calm cream
  body; a loop band into the magazine; then the watch-next row. Every watch page uses this.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign v_line = f[9] | strip
  assign t_clean = v_title | downcase | replace: ',', ' ' | replace: '?', ' ' | replace: '(', ' ' | replace: ')', ' ' | replace: ':', ' '
  assign t_padded = ' ' | append: t_clean | append: ' '
  assign title_post = true
  if t_padded contains ' in '
    assign title_post = false
  endif
  assign cover2 = all_products[section.settings.mag_cover2_handle]
  assign minion_ids = section.settings.loop_minion_ids | default: '35,37,38,10,20,47,26' | split: ','
  assign loop_minion_urls = ''
  for mid in minion_ids
    assign mfile = 'character-' | append: mid | strip | append: '.png'
    assign murl = mfile | asset_img_url: '400x'
    assign loop_minion_urls = loop_minion_urls | append: murl | append: '|'
  endfor
  if v_show == 'picnic'
    assign ground = 'picnic'
  else
    assign ground = 'fieldnotes'
  endif
-%}
{%- liquid
  assign l_who = f[17] | strip
  assign l_needs = f[18] | strip | split: ';;'
  assign l_chapters = f[19] | strip | split: ';;'
  assign l_prompts = f[20] | strip | split: ';;'
  assign l_intask = f[21] | strip | split: ';;'
  assign l_faq = f[22] | strip | split: ';;'
  assign l_opener = f[23] | strip

  comment
    TALK LAYOUT (Ryan, 10 Nov 2026). A Field Notes video is a talk, not a lesson to run, so
    its page is a different way to read the paired field notes post: the video on top, the
    post itself underneath, then the watch-next row and the magazine banner from the
    template. The hero lede carries the summary (so it says something the opener does not),
    the lesson blocks (You'll need, pockets, IN task panel, Run it card) do not render, and
    the chapters heading reads "In this video". Falls back to the lesson layout when the
    talk has no paired post.
  endcomment
  assign is_talk = false
  assign talk_post = nil
  if v_show == 'fieldnotes'
    assign is_talk = true
    if v_post != blank
      assign talk_post_key = 'field-notes/' | append: v_post
      assign talk_post = articles[talk_post_key]
      if talk_post.content == blank
        assign talk_post = nil
      endif
    endif
  endif
  assign lede_text = v_line
  if is_talk
    assign lede_text = v_summary
  endif
  comment
    Blog hero data for the paired post (Ryan, 10 Nov: "fully mimic the blog page"). The same
    reads theinmag-article makes: topic metafield or first tag, author_type picks the byline and
    role (the article section's schema defaults), author_role_override wins the role line,
    quick_answer fills the Quick read card, read time uses the audience wpm table.
  endcomment
  assign talk_topic = ''
  assign talk_byline = ''
  assign talk_role = ''
  assign talk_quick = ''
  assign talk_read = ''
  assign talk_has_cover = false
  if talk_post
    if talk_post.image != blank
      assign talk_has_cover = true
    endif
    assign talk_topic = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.primary_topic
    if talk_topic == blank
      assign talk_topic = talk_post.tags.first
    endif
    assign talk_author = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.author_type | downcase
    if talk_author == 'tam'
      assign talk_byline = 'By Tam B.'
      assign talk_role = 'Classroom teacher & cofounder'
    else
      assign talk_byline = 'By Ryan G.'
      assign talk_role = 'Learning specialist & classroom teacher'
    endif
    assign talk_role_override = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.author_role_override
    if talk_role_override != blank
      assign talk_role = talk_role_override
    endif
    comment
      The article's other two modes, so a guest or kid post never reads "By Ryan G." (Fable check, 10 Nov):
      a kid post shows no byline at all (privacy rule); a guest post reads "Meet [name]." like the blog.
    endcomment
    assign talk_kid = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.kid_first_name
    assign talk_guest = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.guest_name | strip
    if talk_kid != blank
      assign talk_byline = ''
      if talk_role_override == blank
        assign talk_role = ''
      endif
    elsif talk_guest != blank
      assign talk_guest = talk_guest | remove_last: '.'
      assign talk_byline = 'Meet ' | append: talk_guest | append: '.'
    endif
    assign talk_quick = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.quick_answer
    assign talk_audience = talk_post.metafields.field_notes.read_audience | downcase
    if talk_audience == 'kids'
      assign talk_wpm = 125
    elsif talk_audience == 'parents'
      assign talk_wpm = 220
    else
      assign talk_wpm = 170
    endif
    assign talk_words = talk_post.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
    assign talk_minutes = talk_words | times: 1.0 | divided_by: talk_wpm | ceil | at_least: 1
    assign talk_read = talk_minutes | append: ' min read'
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Lesson page v3 (2026-11-07). One template; only the series ground and the main button change.
  Order (reader questions): what is it + is it for me (chips, H1) > the video > how do I run it
  (chapters that jump the player) > what do I ask (pocket questions) > what do I need (Run it card) >
  why it works (How this is an IN task) > transcript + FAQ > then the shop hero banner and watch next.
  Content comes from the registry (fields 17 to 22). Research: WATCH-PAGE-RESEARCH + WATCH-PAGE-SPEC-v1.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="theinmag-video-watch theinmag-video-watch--{{ ground }}" aria-labelledby="theinmag-video-watch-h1">
  <div class="theinmag-video-watch__band"{% if ground == 'fieldnotes' %} style="--vw-pattern: url('{{ 'teacher_backgroundFAQ.jpg' | asset_url }}');"{% endif %}>
    {%- if ground == 'picnic' -%}
      <span class="theinmag-video-watch__decor theinmag-video-watch__decor--rings" aria-hidden="true" style="--decor-mask: url('{{ 'FAQ_HollowCircles.png' | asset_url }}');"></span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="theinmag-video-watch__inner">
      {%- if l_opener != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} Centred Post line saying exactly what this video is (registry field 23; Ryan, 10 Nov: the top under the nav felt bare, handwriting tried and binned). Fades up once; reduced motion shows it still. {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="theinmag-video-watch__opener">{{ l_opener | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="theinmag-video-watch__toprow">
        <nav class="theinmag-video-watch__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/pages/videos">Videos</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
          <a href="{{ show_anchor }}">{{ show_name }}</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <div class="theinmag-video-watch__top">
        <div class="theinmag-video-watch__head">
          {%- comment -%} Logo and the three strips share one row (Ryan, 10 Nov: the logo is big, put the chips down beside it). {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="theinmag-video-watch__brandrow">
            <div class="theinmag-video-watch__brand theinmag-video-watch__brand--head">
              {%- if ground == 'picnic' -%}
                <picture class="theinmag-video-watch__logo theinmag-video-watch__logo--picnic">
                  <source media="(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)" srcset="{{ 'picnic-planning-logo-static.png' | asset_url }}">
                  <img src="{{ 'picnic-planning-logo-anim.webp' | asset_url }}" width="600" height="516" alt="Picnic Planning">
                </picture>
              {%- else -%}
                <img class="theinmag-video-watch__logo theinmag-video-watch__logo--fieldnotes" src="{{ 'fieldnotes_logo_sage.png' | asset_url }}" width="800" height="320" alt="Field Notes">
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
          <h1 id="theinmag-video-watch-h1" class="theinmag-video-watch__title{% unless title_post %} is-inter{% endunless %}">{{ v_title }}</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="theinmag-video-watch__player{% if is_coming %} is-coming{% endif %}" id="lesson-player" data-live-from="{{ v_live_ts }}">
          {%- if is_coming -%}
            <img class="theinmag-video-watch__poster" src="{{ thumb_large }}" width="1280" height="720" fetchpriority="high" alt="Thumbnail for {{ v_title | escape }}">
            <span class="theinmag-video-watch__soon">
              <span class="theinmag-video-watch__soon-big">out {{ v_live_label }}</span>
              <span class="theinmag-video-watch__soon-small">It plays right here once it's live.</span>
            </span>
            <template data-player-template>
              <iframe src="{{ embed_src }}" title="{{ v_title | escape }} (video)" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
            </template>
          {%- else -%}
            <iframe src="{{ embed_src }}" title="{{ v_title | escape }} (video)" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="theinmag-video-watch__act">
          {%- if lede_text != blank -%}<p class="theinmag-video-watch__lede{% if is_talk %} theinmag-video-watch__lede--talk{% endif %}">{{ lede_text }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} Ryan, 10 Nov: the planner and post buttons already live in the Run it card below, so this slot carries the YouTube subscribe link instead (moved down from the breadcrumb row, kept as a small link, not a button). The sitewide footer listener logs it as youtube_click_subscribe. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="theinmag-video-watch__actions">
            <a class="theinmag-video-watch__sub" href="{{ section.settings.sub_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">subscribe on YouTube<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            {%- comment -%} Tam, 10 Nov: the three strips sit in one row under the subscribe link, not beside the logo. {%- endcomment -%}
            <ul class="theinmag-video-watch__chips" aria-label="About this video">
              {%- if v_area != blank -%}<li>{{ v_area }}</li>{%- endif -%}
              <li>{{ v_minutes }}</li>
              {%- if l_who != blank -%}<li>{{ l_who | split: ',' | first | split: '.' | first }}</li>{%- endif -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="theinmag-video-watch__inner theinmag-video-watch__body{% if is_talk %} theinmag-video-watch__body--talk{% endif %}{% if talk_has_cover %} theinmag-video-watch__body--with-cover{% endif %}"{% if talk_has_cover %} data-talk-hero{% endif %}>
    {%- if talk_has_cover -%}
      {%- comment -%} Talk pages read like the blog (Ryan, 10 Nov): the post's cover stays put beside the words on desktop, sits above them on a phone,
        and carries the blog's hero overlay (title, topic, byline, role on a dark scrim) that fades and brightens as the reader scrolls. {%- endcomment -%}
      <aside class="theinmag-video-watch__cover-col">
        <div class="theinmag-video-watch__cover-sticky">
          <img class="theinmag-video-watch__cover-image"
            srcset="{% if talk_post.image.width >= 600 %}{{ talk_post.image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,{% endif %}{% if talk_post.image.width >= 900 %}{{ talk_post.image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,{% endif %}{% if talk_post.image.width >= 1600 %}{{ talk_post.image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w,{% endif %}{{ talk_post.image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w"
            sizes="(min-width: 990px) 50vw, 100vw"
            src="{{ talk_post.image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
            alt="{{ talk_post.image.alt | default: talk_post.title | escape }}" loading="eager" decoding="async" width="{{ talk_post.image.width }}" height="{{ talk_post.image.height }}">
          <div class="theinmag-video-watch__overlay">
            <h2 class="theinmag-video-watch__overlay-title">{{ talk_post.title }}</h2>
            {%- if talk_topic != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-video-watch__overlay-topic">{{ talk_topic }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if talk_byline != blank -%}<p class="theinmag-video-watch__overlay-byline">{{ talk_byline }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            {%- if talk_role != blank -%}<p class="theinmag-video-watch__overlay-role">{{ talk_role }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="theinmag-video-watch__main">
      {%- unless is_talk -%}
      <div class="theinmag-video-watch__about">
        <p class="theinmag-video-watch__summary">{{ v_summary }}</p>
        {%- if v_kid != blank -%}<p class="theinmag-video-watch__credit">{{ v_kid }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- endunless -%}

      {%- comment -%} Chapters are a lesson tool; talks do not list them on the page (Ryan, 10 Nov). The VideoObject Clip schema still carries them. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if is_talk == false and l_chapters.size > 0 and l_chapters[0] != blank -%}
        <h2 class="theinmag-video-watch__h2">How do I run it?</h2>
        <ol class="theinmag-video-watch__chapters">
          {%- for c in l_chapters -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign cp = c | split: '|'
              assign ct = cp[0] | strip
              assign tparts = ct | split: ':'
              assign secs = tparts[0] | times: 60 | plus: tparts[1]
            -%}
            <li><button type="button" class="theinmag-video-watch__chapter" data-seek="{{ secs }}"><span class="theinmag-video-watch__time">{{ ct }}</span><span>{{ cp[1] }}</span></button></li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if l_prompts.size > 0 and l_prompts[0] != blank -%}
        <h2 class="theinmag-video-watch__h2 theinmag-video-watch__h2--pocket">Pocket questions <span>probing questions to keep your kids in flow</span></h2>
        <div class="theinmag-video-watch__pockets">
          {%- for pq in l_prompts -%}
            {%- assign pp = pq | split: '|' -%}
            <div class="theinmag-video-watch__pocket theinmag-video-watch__pocket--{{ pp[0] | strip }}">
              <p class="theinmag-video-watch__pocket-label">{% if pp[0] contains 'stuck' %}If they're stuck{% else %}If they're cruising{% endif %}</p>
              <ul class="theinmag-video-watch__pocket-qs">{%- assign qs = pp[1] | split: '~' -%}{%- for q in qs -%}<li>{{ q | strip }}</li>{%- endfor -%}</ul>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
        {%- if section.settings.pocket_url != blank -%}<p class="theinmag-video-watch__pocket-more"><a class="theinmag-video-watch__textlink" href="{{ section.settings.pocket_url }}">{{ section.settings.pocket_label }} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if l_intask.size > 0 and l_intask[0] != blank -%}
        <aside class="theinmag-video-watch__intask" aria-labelledby="intask-h">
          <span class="theinmag-video-watch__intask-minion" data-loop-minion="{{ loop_minion_urls }}" aria-hidden="true"><img alt="" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" hidden></span>
          <h2 id="intask-h" class="theinmag-video-watch__intask-h">How this is an IN task</h2>
          <dl class="theinmag-video-watch__pillars">
            {%- for it in l_intask -%}
              {%- assign ip = it | split: '|' -%}
              <div><dt>{{ ip[0] }}</dt><dd>{{ ip[1] }}</dd></div>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </dl>
          {%- if section.settings.intask_url != blank -%}
            <a class="theinmag-video-watch__textlink" href="{{ section.settings.intask_url }}">What is an IN task? <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </aside>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if is_talk and talk_post -%}
        <article class="theinmag-video-watch__post">
          {%- unless talk_has_cover -%}
            <p class="theinmag-video-watch__post-eyebrow">The field notes post</p>
            <h2 class="theinmag-video-watch__post-title">{{ talk_post.title }}</h2>
          {%- endunless -%}
          <header class="theinmag-video-watch__post-meta">
            {%- if talk_topic != blank -%}<span class="theinmag-video-watch__post-topic">{{ talk_topic }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            <span>{{ talk_read }}</span>
            {%- if talk_post.published_at != blank -%}<span>{{ talk_post.published_at | date: '%b %-d, %Y' }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          </header>
          {%- if talk_quick != blank -%}
            <aside class="theinmag-video-watch__quick" aria-label="Quick read">
              <span class="theinmag-video-watch__quick-label">Quick read</span>
              <div class="theinmag-video-watch__quick-body rte">{{ talk_quick }}</div>
            </aside>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="theinmag-video-watch__post-body">{{ talk_post.content }}</div>
        </article>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if transcript_html != blank or matched == false -%}
        <details class="theinmag-video-watch__fold">
          <summary>Read the transcript</summary>
          <div class="theinmag-video-watch__fold-body">{% if transcript_html != blank %}{{ transcript_html }}{% else %}<p>Draft preview: the transcript shows here from the page body once this video's own page exists.</p>{% endif %}</div>
        </details>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- for fq in l_faq -%}
        {%- if fq != blank -%}
          {%- assign fp = fq | split: '|' -%}
          <details class="theinmag-video-watch__fold">
            <summary>{{ fp[0] }}</summary>
            <div class="theinmag-video-watch__fold-body"><p>{{ fp[1] }}</p></div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- unless is_talk -%}
    <aside class="theinmag-video-watch__side" aria-label="Run it">
      <div class="theinmag-video-watch__runit">
        <h2 class="theinmag-video-watch__runit-h">Run it</h2>
        {%- if l_needs.size > 0 and l_needs[0] != blank -%}
          <p class="theinmag-video-watch__runit-label">You'll need</p>
          <ul class="theinmag-video-watch__needs">
            {%- for n in l_needs -%}<li>{{ n }}</li>{%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if ground == 'picnic' -%}
          <a class="theinmag-btn theinmag-btn--primary theinmag-video-watch__runit-btn" href="{{ section.settings.planner_url }}">{{ section.settings.planner_label }}</a>
        {%- elsif v_post != blank -%}
          <a class="theinmag-btn theinmag-btn--primary theinmag-video-watch__runit-btn" href="/blogs/field-notes/{{ v_post }}">read the field notes post</a>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="theinmag-video-watch__runit-email"><a href="/pages/newsletter">{{ section.settings.email_line }}</a></p>
      </div>
    </aside>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    /* Chapters jump the embedded YouTube player (enablejsapi=1) and scroll it into view. */
    /* Phones ignore playVideo() until the viewer has tapped play once, so until the player reports
       it has played, a chapter tap reloads the embed at that start time instead. */
    var started = false;
    window.addEventListener('message', function (e) {
      if (typeof e.data !== 'string' || e.data.indexOf('playerState') === -1) return;
      try {
        var d = JSON.parse(e.data);
        if (d.info && d.info.playerState === 1 && !started) {
          started = true;
          /* GA4 youtube_play (2026-11-10): first play of the embed on this page view, once.
             Read by the built-in pagePath dimension like stack_cta_click; video_id needs a
             custom dimension to query. Guarded: analytics never breaks the player. */
          try {
            var pf = document.querySelector('#lesson-player iframe');
            var pm = pf && pf.src ? pf.src.match(/\/embed\/([^?&/]+)/) : null;
            if (typeof window.gtag === 'function') {
              window.gtag('event', 'youtube_play', { video_id: pm ? pm[1] : '', surface: 'watch_page', page_path: window.location.pathname });
            }
          } catch (g) {}
        }
      } catch (x) {}
    });
    var fr = document.querySelector('#lesson-player iframe');
    if (fr) fr.addEventListener('load', function () { fr.contentWindow.postMessage(JSON.stringify({ event: 'listening' }), '*'); });
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-seek]').forEach(function (b) {
      b.addEventListener('click', function () {
        var f = document.querySelector('#lesson-player iframe');
        if (!f) return;
        var t = parseInt(b.getAttribute('data-seek'), 10) || 0;
        if (started) {
          f.contentWindow.postMessage(JSON.stringify({ event: 'command', func: 'seekTo', args: [t, true] }), '*');
          f.contentWindow.postMessage(JSON.stringify({ event: 'command', func: 'playVideo', args: [] }), '*');
        } else {
          f.src = f.src.replace(/&start=\d+/, '').replace(/&autoplay=1/, '') + '&start=' + t + '&autoplay=1';
        }
        document.querySelectorAll('[data-seek].is-current').forEach(function (x) { x.classList.remove('is-current'); });
        b.classList.add('is-current');
        document.getElementById('lesson-player').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      });
    });
  })();
  (function () {
    var slot = document.querySelector('[data-loop-minion]');
    if (!slot) return;
    var urls = slot.getAttribute('data-loop-minion').split('|').filter(Boolean);
    if (!urls.length) return;
    var img = slot.querySelector('img');
    img.src = urls[Math.floor(Math.random() * urls.length)];
    img.hidden = false;
  })();
  (function () {
    var p = document.querySelector('.theinmag-video-watch__player.is-coming');
    if (!p) return;
    var t = parseInt(p.getAttribute('data-live-from'), 10);
    if (!t || Date.now() / 1000 < t) return;
    var tpl = p.querySelector('template[data-player-template]');
    if (!tpl) return;
    p.innerHTML = '';
    p.appendChild(tpl.content.cloneNode(true));
    /* The player script above only found the iframe that existed at load; this one is new, so
       start the jsapi handshake here too, or chapters and youtube_play never hear it (Fable, 10 Nov). */
    var nf = p.querySelector('iframe');
    if (nf) nf.addEventListener('load', function () { nf.contentWindow.postMessage(JSON.stringify({ event: 'listening' }), '*'); });
    p.classList.remove('is-coming');
  })();
  (function () {
    /* Blog hero fade on talk pages (theinmag-article's rule, 10 Nov): --hero-progress runs 0 to 1 over
       the first 30vh the cover column travels past the top of the screen. The overlay fades out and the
       image brightens to natural. Skipped under prefers-reduced-motion (CSS shows everything static). */
    var hero = document.querySelector('[data-talk-hero]');
    if (!hero) return;
    if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    var ticking = false;
    function update() {
      ticking = false;
      var rect = hero.getBoundingClientRect();
      var vh = window.innerHeight || document.documentElement.clientHeight;
      var travel = vh * 0.3;
      if (travel <= 0) return;
      var progress = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, -rect.top) / travel);
      hero.style.setProperty('--hero-progress', progress.toFixed(3));
    }
    function onScroll() { if (!ticking) { window.requestAnimationFrame(update); ticking = true; } }
    window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
    window.addEventListener('resize', onScroll, { passive: true });
    update();
  })();
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": {{ shop.url | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Videos", "item": {{ shop.url | append: '/pages/videos' | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": {{ v_title | json }}, "item": {{ page_url | json }} }
  ]
}
</script>
{%- if is_coming == false -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "VideoObject",
  "name": {{ v_title | json }},
  "description": {{ v_summary | json }},
  "thumbnailUrl": [
    {{ 'https:' | append: thumb_large | json }},
    {{ 'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/' | append: v_id | append: '/maxresdefault.jpg' | json }}
  ],
  "uploadDate": {{ v_live_iso | json }},
  "duration": {{ v_duration | json }},
  "embedUrl": {{ 'https://www.youtube.com/embed/' | append: v_id | json }},
  "url": {{ page_url | json }},
  "inLanguage": "en-AU",
  {%- if l_chapters.size > 0 and l_chapters[0] != blank %}
  "hasPart": [
    {%- for c in l_chapters -%}
      {%- assign cp = c | split: '|' -%}{%- assign tparts = cp[0] | strip | split: ':' -%}{%- assign secs = tparts[0] | times: 60 | plus: tparts[1] -%}
      {%- if forloop.last -%}{%- assign endsecs = v_duration | remove: 'PT' | split: 'M' | first | times: 60 -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign nx = l_chapters[forloop.index] | split: '|' | first | strip | split: ':' -%}{%- assign endsecs = nx[0] | times: 60 | plus: nx[1] -%}{%- endif -%}
      { "@type": "Clip", "name": {{ cp[1] | json }}, "startOffset": {{ secs }}, "endOffset": {{ endsecs }}, "url": {{ watch_url | append: '&t=' | append: secs | json }} }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ],
  {%- endif %}
  "isFamilyFriendly": true,
  "creator": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Ryan", "jobTitle": "Teacher and learning specialist", "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "theINmag" } },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "theINmag",
    "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
    "sameAs": ["https://www.youtube.com/@theINmag"]
  }
  {%- if transcript_html != blank -%},
  "transcript": {{ transcript_html | replace: '</p>', '</p> ' | replace: '<br>', ' ' | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip | json }}
  {%- endif %}
}
</script>
{%- endif -%}

